jobs.description:
Robert Half is currently recruiting a Teamlead (M/F/X)

Our client is an international and well-structured organization with a strong focus on operational excellence, collaboration, and continuous improvement. 

Role

• You support the delivery of high-quality and efficient general accounting services within the shared services environment, including planning, execution, and follow-up of month-end closings and deadlines;
• You assist the team with technical accounting and tax-related questions and help optimize the use of systems, reports, and IT tools;
• You review month-end closings and accounting processes, identify improvement opportunities, and help implement more efficient ways of working;
• You contribute to the development and enhancement of policies related to accounting processes within the shared services structure;
• You play an active role in balance sheet reviews, including follow-up on timing, action points, reporting, and tool harmonization;
• You support ERP implementations and reporting tool roll-outs for the accounting department;
• You help ensure compliance with internal policies, statutory obligations, tax requirements, control standards, and deadlines;
• You maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders and provide a high level of accounting service to internal customers;
• You ensure proper documentation, filing, and control of relevant accounting records and supporting documents;
• You contribute to projects and process optimization initiatives across the department;
• You support team continuity by acting as a back-up for the team lead when needed and by helping organize regular team meetings;
• You provide training, coaching, and technical guidance to colleagues to support team development, service quality, and operational efficiency.

Profile

• You hold a degree in Accounting or an equivalent professional qualification;
• You have at least 5 years of relevant experience in accounting within a professional environment;
• You have a strong command of both Dutch and English, written and spoken;
• You communicate easily with stakeholders at different levels of the organization;
• You are proactive, able to work independently, and confident in taking initiative;
• You are a strong team player and contribute to a positive, service-oriented, and performance-driven culture;
• You think beyond standard solutions, anticipate challenges and opportunities, and focus on continuous improvement;
• You are proficient in Microsoft Office and have solid knowledge of accounting systems and software;
• You combine technical knowledge with a supportive mindset and a customer-focused approach.

To strengthen our Supply Chain Department we are looking for a LOGISTICS TEAM LEADER


Safran Aircraft Engine Services Brussels is a subsidiary of Safran Aircraft Engines, based at Brussels Airport (Zaventem & Steenokkerzeel, Belgium), specialized in the inspection, maintenance and repair (MRO) of the advanced LEAP jet engines that power the latest generation of the Airbus A320NEO & Boeing B737MAX narrow body families. The company is a key player in the integrated CFM international MRO network. With more than 75 years of experience, and up to 20 international Part 145 certifications (EASA/ FAA/ CAAC/ …), Safran Aircraft Engine Services Brussels is recognized as a worldwide center of expertise in the air transport industry. More than a 100 airlines, lessors, private aircraft operators and MRO partners have entrusted their engines to our company. We employ over 500 highly skilled, passionate and enthusiastic employees.


Your role:



• You are a point of contact for our transport partners; 

• You lead a team of 10 logistics colleagues; 

• You provide support for your team by developing their knowledge in cooperation with your manager; 

• You propose relevant KPI's and create reports for the activity; 

• You lead the daily activity meeting together with your manager; 

• You follow the work and safety instructions specifically to the workstation and the company; 

• You respect the internal quality regulations and the rules of logistics and administrative management of the company; 

• You inspire and enthuse employees and stimulate teamwork; 

• You take initiatives and make proposals in a context of continuous improvement, pro-actively evaluates, coordinates the improvement of current work methods and introduces new technologies as they arise; 

• You maintain constructive and effective relations within and outside the company. 

Your profile:

• You hold at least a Bachelor in Supply Chain or Logistics, or a technical education in Logistics with experience, or you have demonstrated experience as a Team Leader;
• You have at least 5 years of experience in team management;
• You demonstrate good communication skills, good practical sense and a sense of initiative while anticipating and taking part in the context of continuous improvement;
• You have a good team spirit and are open and adaptable;
• You speak Dutch, French and are fluent in English;
• You have a good knowledge of IT tools (MS Office + ERP). SAP is a plus

Candidates must be legally authorized to work in Belgium, holding either an EU passport or a valid work & residence permit. Please note that we do not provide assistance with visa or permit applications.
